","type":"text"},{"text":"spawning an entity, and you pass it back to the world to read and change its components:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Ada\"), Health(current: 100))","","print(world[Name.self, of: hero].value)","\/\/ Prints \"Ada\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle is a small value, cheap to copy and store, for example in a component that refers to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another entity. It holds two numbers: the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of the slot the entity occupies in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world, and the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of that slot. When an entity is despawned, the world can reuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its slot for a new entity with the next generation, so a handle kept past its entity’s despawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stale"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it never names the entity that took the slot."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let first = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","world.despawn(first)","let second = world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","","print(first, second)","\/\/ Prints \"0:0 0:1\"","print(world.contains(first))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entities are ordered by slot, then by generation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Operators","generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/_(_:_:)"]},{"title":"I